CORE
main.cpp
--cpp20
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] .* generic lambda: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] .* lambda with a template parameter list: SUCCESS$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
A fold in a lambda over the lambda's own pack, `(f(a), ...)' with f a
parameter of the enclosing function, was reduced as a one-element fold when
the enclosing function's body was prepared: f was called once (with every
element of the pack, or with the first one), without a diagnostic.
